275	// The Bearer flow on the answers Nexus really gave. Two ways in, both measured:
276	//
277	//   - A wrong password. Nexus answers 401 with a BASIC challenge, never a Bearer
278	//     one, so the client does NOT enter the flow: it returns a typed
279	//     *StatusError{401, SourceRegistry} that carries the challenge. No token request
280	//     goes out. imagesearch.Classify turns it into "refused" (access_fixture_test.go).
281	//     Identical on the nominal bench, with the DockerToken realm removed (W5) and
282	//     with the anonymous access cut (W6).
283	//   - An anonymous GET /v2/ (the Docker client's first request). Nexus answers 401
284	//     with a Bearer challenge whose realm is on the registry's own origin; the
285	//     client fetches a token there (200) and retries with it. Nexus answers 401
286	//     AGAIN to that retry: the flow does not succeed on this bench, and the client
287	//     reports the plain 401 of that second answer (it never answers a second
288	//     challenge, and the realm token is not what authorizes a catalog read).
289	//
290	// The Bearer flow therefore never yields a useful read on this Nexus; what the
291	// client does at each step is frozen here.
