644	// Redirects. NX-05 asked whether Nexus ever redirects; the answer measured is no: not
645	// one of the exchanges of the three campaigns carries a 3xx or a Location, whatever
646	// the candidate that was tried (GET /v2 without its slash, /repository/<r>/v2 without
647	// its slash, /v2/<repo>, the HEAD of a manifest and the GET of a blob on the hosted
648	// repository). The answers are direct: 200, 401 Bearer, or a 404 page. So there is no
649	// redirect to follow and none off the origin to refuse, and this test pins the direct
650	// answers (the client takes each as it is: one request, no hop).
651	//
652	// The refusal of a redirect or a Link off the origin is NOT measured (the bench has no
653	// reverse proxy and its blob store is a file one). It stays covered, and only, by the
654	// tests written by hand: TestRegistryRedirectOffOriginSendsNoCredentials,
655	// TestRegistryRedirectRoundTripRefused and TestRegistryRedirectRefusalDoesNotLeakTarget
656	// (registry_origin*_test.go), TestListRegistryTagsNextOffOriginIsAnError,
